<main>
    <div class="roadmap-header fade-up fade-up-1">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="dates">Last updated 2026-10-28 &middot; plain-language beta privacy policy &mdash; a lawyer hasn't blessed these yet</p>
    </div>

    <section class="section fade-up fade-up-2">
        <p>Parachute exists so your thoughts have a private place to live. That only works if you can trust what happens to them. This page says, plainly, what <strong>Open Parachute, PBC</strong> (a Colorado Public Benefit Corporation) stores and what we will never do with it. Questions to <a href="mailto:hello@parachute.computer">hello@parachute.computer</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>What we store</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Your email address</strong> &mdash; it's how you sign in (magic links) and how we reach you.</li>
            <li><strong>The notes you write</strong> &mdash; your vault's contents, stored so we can show them back to you and back them up. We don't read them except when you explicitly ask us to help debug something, or when the law compels us.</li>
            <li><strong>Usage metrics</strong> &mdash; basics like storage used and when your vault was last active. Enough to run the service and see what's working; no tracking you around the web. (If we add page analytics to this website, it will be cookieless and anonymous, and we'll update this page when we do.)</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>What we don't do</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>We don't sell your data.</strong> Not to advertisers, not to brokers, not to anyone. Our business is a service you pay for (free during the open beta), full stop.</li>
            <li><strong>We don't train AI on your vault.</strong> We don't use your notes to train any AI model, and we don't send them to an outside AI company. A few features do run AI models on our side &mdash; see <a href="#ai-on-our-side">AI that runs on our side</a> below. When <em>you</em> connect your own AI to your vault, that's your choice and your AI.</li>
            <li><strong>We don't run ads</strong> and we don't use advertising trackers.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="ai-on-our-side">
        <h2>AI that runs on our side</h2>
        <p>To make some features work, Parachute Cloud runs AI models inside Cloudflare (Workers AI), the same company that already hosts your vault, on our account:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Voice memos.</strong> When you record one, a speech-to-text model (Whisper) turns it into text, and a language model tidies the transcript (punctuation, paragraphs). The raw transcript is always kept next to the tidied one.</li>
            <li><strong>Search by meaning.</strong> An embedding model reads your notes to build the index that lets search find a note by what it means, not just the words in it.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>These models run only to provide those features, and what they produce is stored in your vault. We don't use your notes to train them or any other model.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>Who else touches the data (subprocessors)</h2>
        <p>We keep the list short:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> &mdash; hosts the service, stores vault data and backups, and runs the AI models above (Workers AI) on our behalf.</li>
            <li><strong>Stripe</strong> &mdash; processes payments for paid plans. New paid plans are paused during the open beta. Stripe sees your payment details; we never store your card number.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If this list grows, we'll update this page before the new subprocessor handles your data.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>Email we send</h2>
        <p>Signing in works by <strong>magic link</strong>, so you'll get an email each time you sign in &mdash; that one's unavoidable. Beyond that, new accounts get a short <strong>three-email onboarding series</strong> (a welcome, a "connect your AI?" nudge, and a feedback ask), and we may occasionally send service announcements that affect your account. Every non-essential email has an unsubscribe link, and unsubscribing is honored immediately. No marketing lists, no partner emails.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="deleting-your-data">
        <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
        <p>Delete a vault and it goes: every note, tag and link, its attachment files, its nightly snapshots and its export files. Delete your account and every vault you own goes that way, along with your account records (sign-in sessions, tokens, connected apps, usage records and the account itself) and your Stripe customer record if you had one (any subscription is cancelled first). Account deletion has a 24-hour undo window; after that it's permanent.</p>
        <p>Three things outlast a deletion for a while: our hosting platform's own backups of the database and storage age out within about 30 days; operational logs, which carry account ids but never note content, age out on their own short retention; and Stripe keeps the invoices and payment records that tax law requires it to keep.</p>
        <p>Want everything gone, or a copy of everything we hold about you? Email <a href="mailto:hello@parachute.computer">hello@parachute.computer</a> and we'll do it &mdash; no forms, no retention tricks. And you can <a href="/terms/">export everything yourself</a> at any time, no permission needed.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>If this policy changes in a way that matters, we'll update the date at the top and email registered users before the change takes effect. See also our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>.</p>
    </section>
</main>
